   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "SRM = Widdel & Bak (1992) marine defined sulfate-reducer medium, applied as an anoxic sediment slurry (10% sediment / 90% SRM) with petroleum n-alkanes (C5-C14) as sole carbon/electron source and sulfate as electron acceptor, 70 C, N2:CO2 (90:10) headspace. The ref-65 Nat. Protoc. PDF is paywalled, so exact bulk-salt/buffer/reductant concentrations were taken from the Widdel & Bak marine medium it reproduces, and the named SL-10, selenite-tungstate and 10-vitamin stock solutions were expanded from DSMZ MediaDive 383 (same Widdel lineage). Trace-metal/vitamin values are stock-solution amounts; "
